      "q": "3. A few exercises with dates:\nPlace these dates chronologically on the timeline: 323 CE, 323 BCE, 100 CE, 100 BCE, 1900 BCE, 1090 CE, 2024 CE.",
      "a": "1900 BCE\n323 BCE\n100 BCE\n100 CE\n323 CE\n1090 CE\n2024 CE\nIf King Chandragupta was born in 320 CE, which century did he belong to? And how many years was that after the Buddha\u2019s birth?\nAns:\nKing Chandragupta was born in the 4th century CE (320 CE).\nBuddha was born around 563 BCE, so the difference between Buddha\u2019s birth and Chandragupta\u2019s birth is approximately 883 years (563 BCE + 320 CE).\nRani of Jhansi was born in 1828. Which century did she belong to? How many years was that before India\u2019s Independence?\nAns:\nRani of Jhansi was born in the 19th century (1828).\nIndia gained independence in 1947, so Rani of Jhansi\u2019s birth was 119 years before India\u2019s independence (1947 - 1828 = 119).\nTurn \u201812,000 years ago\u2019 into a date.\nAns:\n12,000 years ago from the present (2024 CE) would be around 10,000 BCE (2024 CE - 12,000 years = 10,000 BCE)."
