      "q": "4. Plan a visit to a nearby museum: the visit should be prepared with some prior research on the kind of exhibits the museum holds. Keep notes during the visit. Write a brief report afterward, highlighting what was unexpected/interesting/fun about the visit and the exhibits.",
      "a": "Date of Visit\n: 12th September 2024\nMuseum Name\n: National History Museum\nExhibits Viewed\n:\nDuring my visit, I explored a variety of exhibits, including artefacts from ancient India, sculptures, and historical tools. The most fascinating section was dedicated to the Indus Valley Civilization, where I saw seals, pottery, and tools used by early settlers. Another highlight was the collection of mediaeval Indian coins, which helped me understand the economic systems of ancient times.\nUnexpected Findings\n:\nOne unexpected exhibit was a collection of early human fossils, which showed the development of humans over thousands of years. I didn\u2019t expect to see actual fossil remains of animals like mammoths, which added a new dimension to the experience.\nFun Aspects\n:\nThe interactive displays were quite enjoyable. One section allowed visitors to digitally recreate ancient pottery, which was both fun and educational. There were also 3D models of ancient structures that provided a closer look at how ancient cities were built.\nThis visit was both informative and enjoyable, giving me a deeper understanding of ancient cultures and their ways of life."
